  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Calm weather conditions expected to\ncontinue over the next several days with warming temperatures\ntoday and tomorrow as highs reach several degrees above normal. By\nFriday and over the weekend, a low pressure to the northwest will\nmove into the northwestern CONUS which will tighten weather\ngradients above Nevada which will increase winds in the afternoons\nfor Friday and Saturday along with much cooler temperatures. Winds\non Friday are expected around 10-15 mph with gusts up to 25-35\nmph, with Saturday winds expected to be stronger with speeds up to\n20-25 mph sustained and gusts up to 35-45 mph. Fire Weather Watch\nhas been issued across all zones Saturday as minimum relative\nhumidity will drop below 15% with the strong winds. The low\npressure system will also drag much cooler air into Nevada with\nhighs reaching to near normal Saturday, then dropping to several\ndegrees below normal on Sunday. Into the next week, temperatures\nwill slightly warm but expected to stay around normal with light\nwinds.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence for warming\ntemperature trends today and tomorrow. Moderate confidence for\nstrong gusty winds and cooler temperatures over the weekend. No\nchanges to NBM grids at this time.",
